# Reference lab (.github/workflows/reference-lab.yml): what a push runs.
# The plan and its rules: BACKLOG §0 "Reference lab"; skill ui-design §4
# (MX is a reference for proportions and behaviour, never for looks).
#
# 22 Nov 2026: fetch the MX Player the owner has on the phone (installed
# from the Play Store, version 3.4.3, read off the phone's App info) and keep
# it in the private repository innocent-ref. Nothing to compare with yet.
#   run 44984807250: innocent-ref reached (private); listed Google Play,
#     apkeep 1.1.0's default source, not APKPure.
#   run 44985066077: APKPure lists 63 versions (1.85.8 to 3.5.3), 3.4.3
#     among them; no x86_64 build of it. Run 3: arm64-v8a, x86_64 optional.
#   run 44985566401: 3.4.3 arm64-v8a and 1.85.8 downloaded; the base APK did
#     not verify (apksigner). Run 4 prints apksigner's reason.
#   run 44985917683: it VERIFIES (v2, v3; signer CN=Kim Jae hyun, O=MX
#     Technologies) with a verified Google Play source stamp. The script
#     read "Signer #1"; build-tools 37 prints "V3.0 Signer:". Run 5: both
#     read, and the Play stamp required.
#
# 22 Nov 2026 (later): MODE=probe — does MX 3.4.3 (native code for
# arm64-v8a only) run on an x86_64 image that translates ARM? First
# google_apis API 30 (Android 11), where Innocent's own libs once died on a
# SIMD instruction inside libndk_translation; another translating API if
# not. Sized like the owner's phone (1080x2316, 450 dpi, three-button nav,
# punch hole); MX's network cut by uid; our own measuring film. Compare
# with nothing yet: this run says whether Phase 1 can use the emulator.
#   run 44989031141: MX 3.4.3 INSTALLS on API 30 (base, arm64 split,
#     xxxhdpi; primary ABI arm64-v8a under translation). The film's intent
#     with -p brought Android's "Open with" chooser (MX has a player and a
#     pop-up player) and MX never ran. Run 2 names the player activity.
#   run 44989696334: MX's native code loads through the translator
#     ("Initialized NDK translation (aarch64)"), no SIGILL. But it opened the
#     PiP activity (first by name) and MX showed its own storage screen
#     (READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE alone is not enough for it); the first-run
#     tapper chose its "not now" and MX left. Run 3: the player activity in
#     Android's order, not pop-up/PiP; "All files access" allowed (appops).
#   run 44990303466: PHASE 0 PASSES. MX's player (ActivityScreen) opened
#     the film offline, controls up, resumed 1, alive 1, SIGILL 0, fatal 0;
#     779 packets MX tried were refused (the uid cut holds). MX turned
#     itself sideways. uiautomator never found MX's player idle (10 s
#     timeouts), so its tree now comes from dumpsys (ui.py hier).
#
# 22 Nov 2026 (later still): MODE=panels — Phase 1. MX and Innocent's
# x86_64 lab build of this commit, the ⋮, ♪ and CC panels, upright and
# sideways (the lab fixes the rotation: wm set-fix-to-user-rotation), over
# a black and a white frame; tool/ref/measure.py and compare.py. Compare
# with nothing earlier: the first measurement.
#   run 44991688519: no panel measured; three faults of the lab's, each
#     fixed. dumpsys activity top lists the launcher's task first and the
#     tree was taken from it (ui.py hier now takes PACKAGE's). Innocent's
#     libmpv stalled on the emulator's goldfish H.264 decoder ("Playback
#     failed"): the lab now sets Innocent's own Development switch,
#     software decoding. Turning MX upright from outside squeezed its
#     controls into a band: upright now uses an upright film (720x1280) and
#     each app turns itself. And MX's controls were still up 12 s after an
#     open, so the lab's tap hid them: the tree is now checked before a tap.
#   run 44994060537: 7 panel screens; MX's CC panel sideways measured (a
#     right-side panel, 47 % wide, full height, controls away). Innocent
#     now plays (software). Faults: MX's shortcut row, moved down by a
#     translation the dump does not show, read as the top bar (its toolbar
#     menu now names the buttons); MX's ⋮ panel came after the screen was
#     taken (now waited for in the tree); Innocent's controls hid while
#     uiautomator read them (both apps are now paused first: paused, the
#     controls stay); MX kept the upright film sideways or never showed
#     its controls (each screen now notes the way the app turned).
MODE=panels
MX_PACKAGE=com.mxtech.videoplayer.ad
MX_VERSION=3.4.3
# MX's signing certificate (SHA-256), read in run 44985917683 from 3.4.3,
# whose Google Play source stamp verified. Any later version fetched must
# carry the same.
MX_CERT=0d9b4c778672e753d45aba4f10df31e1d10bf75b1245469131ef01b82f0f91b6
# The file MODE=probe installs: the release mx-<version> of innocent-ref,
# its size and SHA-256 as GitHub recorded them at upload (get_release_by_tag,
# 22 Nov). probe.sh refuses any other file.
MX_ASSET=mx-3.4.3-arm64-v8a.xapk
MX_SIZE=67788927
MX_SHA256=6f877a3d482e2213b9abb25a0a8c6497e036181339aa1540d21e5635ef4a13bf
# The emulator for MODE=probe: an x86_64 image that translates ARM, and the
# owner's screen (about 384x823 dp).
PROBE_API=30
PROBE_TARGET=google_apis
PROBE_SIZE=1080x2316
PROBE_DPI=450
